      "title": "Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer as growth removed during surgery",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/pope-leo-hospital-operation-growth-lung",
      "description": "<p>Vatican says pontiff had lower lobe of right lung removed in ‘successful, on schedule and as planned’ operation in Rome</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/pope-leo-xiv\">Pope Leo</a> has lung cancer, the Vatican said late on Tuesday.</p><p>Leo, 71, underwent an operation and had the lower lobe of his right lung removed, with tests confirming a diagnosis of lung adenocarcinoma, the Vatican said in a medical bulletin, which followed an earlier statement saying the pope’s operation had concluded “successfully, on schedule and as planned”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/pope-leo-hospital-operation-growth-lung\">Continue reading...</a>",
