      "description": "Pope Leo XIV's surgery confirmed that he has lung cancer and he had the lower lobe of his right lung removed, the Vatican said Tuesday.\nThe tests confirmed a diagnosis of lung adenocarcinoma, the Vatican said in a medical bulletin after the surgery. It said the diagnosis had been suspected by preoperative tests and was confirmed during surgery.\nThe 71-year-old was in the operating room for about 3 hours, the statement said. The surgery itself lasted approximately 90 minutes. \"The surgery was successful, and there were no complications,\" the statement said.\nPope Leo XIV underwent surgery Tuesday to remove a lung nodule and the Vatican said the operation was completed \"successfully, on schedule and as planned.\"\nThe 71-year-old Leo returned to his room after the surgery at Rome's Gemelli hospital, according to a statement from the Vatican spokesperson, who promised further information at a later time.\nLeo had walked into Rome's Gemelli hospital through the main entrance earlier in th",
